1
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:31,409
This is Khun Chai Phakdee.

2
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,443
From now on, he will be your fiancé.

3
00:00:48,170 --> 00:00:49,575
Greetings, Lady Rinkham.

4
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:51,907
My name is Phakdee.

5
00:00:53,450 --> 00:00:56,147
Dad, are you trying to force me into an arranged marriage? I won't accept this.

6
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:01,255
What did you just say?

7
00:01:01,610 --> 00:01:03,495
I do not accept this engagement.

8
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:04,467
I refuse.

9
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:06,356
You are being impolite.

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,421
But I never asked you to control my life, Dad.

11
00:01:11,010 --> 00:01:12,603
I have already made up my mind about this.

12
00:01:13,796 --> 00:01:15,790
I want to find someone to take care of you.

13
00:01:16,510 --> 00:01:18,289
But I already have Kaew.

14
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:24,547
Kaew won't be with you forever, Rinkham.

15
00:01:26,650 --> 00:01:27,938
But I haven't chosen yet.

16
00:01:28,670 --> 00:01:30,953
But you ought to know your duty.

17
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:32,972
I know it well,

18
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:35,630
and I will choose for myself who I love

19
00:01:35,667 --> 00:01:37,126
and want to marry.

20
00:01:37,530 --> 00:01:39,206
Not have you chosen for me, Dad.

21
00:02:43,620 --> 00:02:45,938
But you ought to know your duty.

22
00:02:46,760 --> 00:02:47,883
I know it well,

23
00:02:48,650 --> 00:02:50,560
and I will choose for myself who I love

24
00:02:50,590 --> 00:02:52,080
and want to marry.

25
00:02:52,530 --> 00:02:54,221
Not have you chosen for me, Dad.

26
00:02:59,033 --> 00:02:59,704
Rinkham...

27
00:03:00,710 --> 00:03:01,840
I can't accept this.

28
00:03:02,070 --> 00:03:03,618
I don't want a life like that.

29
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,686
I want to choose the person I love myself

30
00:03:06,790 --> 00:03:09,058
and I already know who that is.

31
00:03:13,050 --> 00:03:14,350
Then what are you going to do?

32
00:03:16,570 --> 00:03:18,030
I'll make dad see

33
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:21,993
that I'm completely unfit to be a bride for anyone he picks.

34
00:03:22,750 --> 00:03:24,996
If that "Khun Chai" guy can tolerate me, then let him try!

35
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:44,498
Rinkham, come here for a moment, my child.

36
00:03:44,830 --> 00:03:46,209
I’m going outside with Kaew.

37
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:47,378
But I have something to…

38
00:03:47,396 --> 00:03:48,590
Let’s save it for another day, sir.

39
00:03:56,230 --> 00:03:59,181
Around that time, she was very close with those guards, wasn't she?

40
00:04:00,430 --> 00:04:01,052
Yes, sir.

41
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:28,467
Why do you come to the market every day?

42
00:04:29,530 --> 00:04:31,200
I don't want to go back home to see my dad.

43
00:04:39,090 --> 00:04:41,532
I’ve figured out what we should do!

44
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:56,350
Is this piece good?

45
00:04:57,540 --> 00:04:58,707
Let's choose for yourself.

46
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:02,166
I want you to choose it,

47
00:05:02,950 --> 00:05:06,295
because sometimes… you are the one who has to take it off.

48
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:12,855
This color suits you.

49
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:15,550
I don't need to…

50
00:05:15,569 --> 00:05:16,338
Want to try it on?

51
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:19,206
I am a guard.

52
00:05:20,590 --> 00:05:22,104
I don't need to wear this.

53
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,655
What are you doing to Rinkham?!

54
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:28,203
Rinkham!

55
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:34,996
Don't move.

56
00:05:36,430 --> 00:05:38,276
You have great taste, my lady.

57
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:50,123
	Here, turn around and let me see.

58
00:06:03,390 --> 00:06:06,541
It’s not the kind of clothing I’m used to wearing.

59
00:06:09,230 --> 00:06:12,553
My lady, your guard is blushing.

60
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:17,956
I've never seen you like this before.

61
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:19,796
And you shouldn't be seeing it either.

62
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,153
But I think it's beautiful.

63
00:06:28,940 --> 00:06:30,172
That's enough.

64
00:06:30,650 --> 00:06:32,769
Not yet. Turn around one more time.

65
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:34,301
Rinkham...

66
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:55,809
You should wear things like this more often.

67
00:07:04,110 --> 00:07:04,990
Never.

68
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:09,273
Auntie, aren't those two acting way too close for master and servant?

69
00:07:09,780 --> 00:07:10,689
That's what I'm saying.

70
00:07:10,713 --> 00:07:13,150
I wonder if they're guards and masters, or actually lovers.

71
00:07:13,810 --> 00:07:15,144
They don't look like a master and servant at all.

72
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:17,335
This really isn't proper.

73
00:07:17,730 --> 00:07:18,590
Hey.

74
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:20,418
My Lady.

75
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:25,913
Please don't cause a scene.

76
00:07:26,730 --> 00:07:27,796
I beg you.

77
00:07:36,578 --> 00:07:37,833
Let's go back, My Lady.

78
00:07:39,650 --> 00:07:41,446
I don't want to go home yet, Kaew.

79
00:07:42,630 --> 00:07:44,344
Your dad will get worried.

80
00:07:47,710 --> 00:07:49,015
You two sure are close.

81
00:07:49,624 --> 00:07:51,620
I heard people in the market gossiping about it...

82
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:55,347
Master and servant, or something more?

83
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:57,667
And what does that have to do with you?

84
00:07:59,530 --> 00:08:02,387
I just don't like seeing things that are unnatural.

85
00:08:02,890 --> 00:08:06,806
because soon enough, certain important people might start getting upset about it.

86
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:08,990
If so, then don't look.

87
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:11,076
You got a big mouth!

88
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:21,138
It seems you are the one acting out of line right now.

89
00:08:23,009 --> 00:08:24,123
Stay away from her.

90
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:30,510
Otherwise, I might not be this kind next time.

91
00:08:31,286 --> 00:08:32,246
Alright, alright.

92
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:41,846
Are you angry?

93
00:08:46,264 --> 00:08:48,843
I just don't like anyone speaking about you like that.

94
00:08:50,690 --> 00:08:52,498
No matter what the truth may be.

95
00:08:55,020 --> 00:08:57,809
But I like it when you protect me.

96
00:08:58,690 --> 00:09:02,400
Or should I let him say it again?

97
00:09:02,690 --> 00:09:03,956
So you can protect me one more time.

98
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,486
Rinkham.

99
00:09:07,870 --> 00:09:09,089
I'm just kidding.

100
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:12,658
But I really do like it when you protect me, you know.

101
00:09:13,450 --> 00:09:15,661
You are quite charming.

102
00:09:29,660 --> 00:09:30,916
Let us return, My Lady.
